WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.890
Dental data are the great absentees of the
European Health Data Space.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:12.550
Not for lack of value, but because of
how dentistry is organised.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.550
Across Europe, most practices are small
businesses with their own software.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.270
In some countries public insurance
pays for dental care;

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:25.630
in others, families and private
insurers pay almost everything.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:29.190
We studied eight countries and
found two funding models,

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:34.250
and none of them has yet formally
designated its health data access body.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:38.570
In nearly all of them, clinical dental
data stay in each practice,

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:43.250
with no registry for adults and no link
to national health records.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.950
The data exist, they are abundant,

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.710
and their owners have reasons to
share them under control.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.710
What is missing is someone
to connect them.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:55.200
That is Dental Data.
